A||||9||Refio||how do you get to back row of plugs on V6?
Z||000000||Refio||05-09-99||07:19 AM||||Would like to do my own tune-up on my GT, but haven't a clue on how to get to the 3 plugs in the back row? Little help! TIA!
Z||000001||Rob||05-09-99||07:36 AM||||With a three inch extension, and a couple of skinned fingers. 
Z||000002||Eric||05-09-99||10:26 AM||||I think I used a six inch extension and a universal joint.  Oh yeah, also wore gloves...hehe.
Z||000003||RFMike||05-09-99||04:17 PM||||i just put plugs in my gt.  the guy at the parts store convinced me to try the bosch platinum plugs.  an added benefit for me was that the four conductors guided the plugs into the holes.  i couldn't believe how much easier it was to get the plugs in the holes. i don't have feeling in my right hand, and it was still easy.  30 bucks was a lot of money.  hope i get some increase in hp and mileage.  even if i don't, it might have been worth it.  by the way, the left rear plug looked like it hadn't been changed in the last century.  different brand than the other five, too.  the guy i bought it from had a garage do all his maintainance.  another reason for changing them.
Z||000004||Howard||05-10-99||02:00 PM||||Remove Trunk Lid takes 5min, gives losts of room to get at back plugs, should take less than 10 mins to replace plugs and another 5 mins to put trunk back on, did this last weekend.
Z||000005||Cliff Pennock||05-10-99||03:00 PM||||RFMike, I'm very curious to hear if those Bosch plugs really make any difference. I've been considering using them as well, but couldn't find anyone yet who had used them.
Z||000006||theogre||05-11-99||09:00 AM||||just watch using them in engines with DIS systems.... I've been hearing notes about the platinums burning back the center electrode. I put in some Split Fire plugs in my 87 DIS 4cyl, so far no problem with those.
Z||000007||Howard||05-11-99||11:02 AM||||The plugs i just put in are AC Rapidfire, they do what they say, the motor runs smoother, and pulls harder, i`d say i got a 5-10hp increase,this motor was rebuilt last fall and only has 500 miles on it, all new<br>Accel Cap, rotor, 8.8 Wires and AC Delco Plugs where put in then and so just changing<br>the plugs all the benefit goes to them.
Z||000008||RFMike||05-11-99||03:38 PM||||Cliff,<br>as it happens, i just got back from a 250 mile site inspection trip.  mileage was 2 mpg better, and the car pulls slightly harder.  this isn't really a fair test, though, because of the rear plugs being in such bad shape (see earlier).  one of the wires had a knick in it, and they weren't a matched set, so i replaced them. this defitely should have helped, regardless of plug type.<br>Ogre,<br>where did you read about bosch plugs?  now you've got me wondering.
Z||000009||PaUL||05-11-99||05:35 PM||||I think Ogre is talking about the older single platinum electrod bosch plugs. You have the new 4 electrode type right? The DIS puts out a reverse polarity spark on some plugs and this is what causes the problems.
